+# CONTRACT — Beam Splitter
+
+## countBeamCells(grid): number
+
+- [ ] Source cell counts as visited → grid with just S: returns 1
+- [ ] Beam travels straight down marking each cell → vertical column counted
+- [ ] Splitter cell hit by beam counts as visited
+- [ ] After splitter, both diagonal cells counted
+- [ ] Cell counted once even if multiple beams pass through it (example 2 → 6)
+- [ ] Example 1 → 5
+- [ ] Example 2 → 6
+- [ ] Beams leaving grid boundaries are not counted (out of bounds absorbed)
+- [ ] Empty grid (no S) → 0
+- [ ] Multiple sources on top row → union of visited cells
+- [ ] Diagonal beam continues diagonally until it exits or hits splitter
+- [ ] Splitter splits regardless of incoming direction (diagonal beam into splitter)
+
+## countBeamPaths(grid): bigint
+
+- [ ] No splitter, single straight beam → 1n
+- [ ] One splitter → 2n (example 1)
+- [ ] Example 2 → 4n
+- [ ] K splitters in a chain → 2^K paths
+- [ ] Absorbed beams (exit out of side) still count as a completed path
+- [ ] No source → 0n
+- [ ] Multiple sources → sum of paths
+- [ ] Returns bigint type
+- [ ] Large result correct (deep splitter chain produces astronomically large bigint)
+
+## Performance
+
+- [ ] 200x200 grid, 50 splitters → both functions return in < 5s
+
+## Quality
+
+- [ ] npm run build clean
+- [ ] npm run lint clean
+- [ ] npm test all pass
